\pard\plain \li540\fi-270\ltrch\loch \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\pard\plain \ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 "How long do you think it will take them to figure out the green room" Said John, looking over to Tebo. Tebo seemed unbothered, overcome with excitement for what lay ahead. "It served its purpose" he concluded. Doesn't matter "What's more important right now is this girls signature". Tebo paned through a series of burn plumes on the ships overhead display \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93There we are\u8230\'85 standard export carrier plume for the exit region\u8230\'85 check\u8221\'94 The ships chaotic burn hummed and churned with strange sounds easing off to a once again steady less chaotic burn, "Can't hide from\u8217\'92em on an exit burns power draw, the cloak tech draws to much energy from the drive\u8230\'85 may as well fool them!\u8221\'94 Tebos visor lit up in what seemed like a smile as he turned back to the others. I've set our drive signature to match haulers in the region.}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "scrivcmt://50082236-582D-47B6-AB94-A1F34A2624C4"}{\fldrslt\f0\fs24\b0\i0  By the time we come in visual range of the blockade, we can actuate our cloaking technology. }}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Suddenly the violent vibrations through the ship simmered down to a soft hum. }{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "scrivcmt://010363C8-AB75-4B78-B337-90EA5FFA7E96"}{\fldrslt\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93We\u8217\'92ve just entered the stratosphere, Engines running silent. Electrical systems and vitals kept to a minimum. She\u8217\'92s cold."}}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Over in the co-pilot's seat, John seemed uneasy. He couldn't piece together how passing the Protectant blockade would be so easy. He knew Tor,  of his engineering prowess. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93The Sparrow from our earlier encounter, Tau did you get a chance to pull it\u8217\'92s logs.. any outgoing transmissions about the Sentient cloaking tech it encountered on the ground? It won't take much for their sensors counter new tech, the engineers could have patched it. I would suggest setting cloak frequency to a different transform, they could be searching that frequency for anomalies\u8221\'94.  Tau looked in John\u8217\'92s direction" Since when did you take up my anxiety issues" John looked back at her then turned back looking up to his terminal. "Just a gut feeling\u8221\'94}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I get it, you\u8217\'92ve only been pulled out of the shit once by me..\u8221\'94 Tebo joked sarcastically \u8220\'93The cloaking technology itself is different to that used in Earth\u8217\'92s atmosphere. I\u8217\'92ll remind you that sound doesn\u8217\'92t travel the same in space, well not at all.. Fooling light in space requires a more.. Physical disguising mechanism\u8221\'94. \u8220\'93It\u8217\'92s impressive\u8221\'94 Said Tau, locking into her helmet left arm followed by her right. \u8220\'93Thanks lefty\u8221\'94 Tebo remarked. }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93It\u8217\'92s too quiet they should have hailed us by now, what\u8217\'92s the fucking hold up!\u8221\'94 Tau seemed nervous like she had been on the observing end of the bridge before when others had been caught out trying to seek economical asylum in the belt from economic threshold sectors.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 "I'm starting the vacuum preparations, I want hull breach measures at the ready" John concluded as he keyed his terminal into autopilot, raising it from around his shoulders over his head in one swift motion, The command console neatly tucking into the roof out of the way. He rose from his seat and moved toward the cargo hold with quick, calculated steps. }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The others unstrapped from their G seats. Tau was first followed by Tex then Shai. They carried the weight of John\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s judgment out like assumed orders without question or doubt, calmly making their way to the cargo hold where their freshly serviced and upgraded mark IV's waited. \u8220\'93Mark SP1\u8221\'94 Tebo had termed his modifications.  }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Their boots clamped to the deck clanking one after the other. All was still and quiet as though they were all clanking around a floating tin can. John was the first to make it to his suit in the cargo hold wings splayed out with the others. I vats of the cargo hold had been supplied with the same gelatinous fluid that the suit's neuro-link jump suits synchronised with The suits all lined the cargo hold leant over like sleeping angels }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 John adjusted his suit and looked over at Tebo in the cockpit, calm as ever.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 "You\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92re sure these signals are clean, right? Last thing we need is a surprise rail slug through the hull right now."}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Tebo barely glanced up from the console, fingers tapping effortlessly. "Clean as they come. Focus on your vacuum prep. If anything does happen, we\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92ll be ready."}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Tex grinned from the back, already locked in. The back of his suit reached around his back locking him in holding him up firmly. He was facing the outer hull, veering out the cloaked cargo hull, leaning against the wall. It almost seemed real. Tebo had coded the reflective transparent nano magnetic field of nanobots to reflect one micro panelled side to the onlookers.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93The cloaking technology itself is different to that used in Earth\u8217\'92s atmosphere. As you all know sound does not travel in space\u8221\'94. \u8220\'93It\u8217\'92s impressive\u8221\'94 Said Tau, locking into her helmet left arm followed by her right. \u8220\'93Thanks lefty\u8221\'94 Tebo remarked. }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0  When Tex veered out of the ship, an algorithm in his helmet rendered it almost seamless. As he veered through the cold shell of the helmets visor. They all took a moment to appreciate the difference in viewpoint through the helmet. Where the strangely reflected angles of the nanobots all but vanished from the close view point of the ships occupant within. When they put their heads into there helmets they felt at ease. Tau hoped that the Sentient technology was as good as he claimed it to be. She trusted Tebo\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s confidence in the way he explained the technology. His voice strong and firm with rigour.    }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 "Ain\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t nothin\u8217\'92 ready for a railgun slug through the hull, though. You sure that fancy energy converter\u8217\'92s gonna save your hide if we spring a leak?" Tebo turned, unphased, raising an eyebrow. "if a slug hits the hull big guy, you'll be changing fuel cells before you have time to worry about my converter.", John interviened. \u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ll get the shells, Tex up top if it comes to that, I want you on the Rail gun support with Tebo if they open fire\u8221\'94. }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Shai had just finished checking her bio gel reserves. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93If you take a round big guy no sweat, just don\u8217\'92t get domed hey\u8230\'85. The logistics of getting in touch with your sleeve, isn\u8217\'92t really an option last I checked\u8221\'94. Tau gave a timeline of return, \u8220\'93Oasis is a long haul away from protectant jurisdiction according to Tebo, but the carrier get us there in time if anyone gets hurt fast enough\u8221\'94. John nodded to Tau then Tex pitched in with a smugness. \u8220\'93Marcellus I am sure would love to interrogate you if you tried jumping back in one of your sleeves\u8221\'94. }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Tau smiled as though she was up to something as the words expired from Tex\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s lips. "Well, that's comforting." John adjusted his helmet, his tone half-joking but his movements precise. "At least we won't be sucked through a pinhole, right?"}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Tebo finally smirked, the closest he ever came to a joke. "No, John. Your guts will remain intact. All the equipment too. Just don\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t take a round to the calf. I don\u8217\'92t know how useful you will be if your boots maglock cell takes a round, ever tried fighting in zero G?" John seemed confident, \u8220\'93Won\u8217\'92t be the first time\u8221\'94 He cocked back the chamber on his Sherpa rifle, then checked the ammo reserve banks for his suit.   }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Tebo tuned back to his console, the faint hum of the vacuum system starting up. "And before you ask, yes\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 we\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92ll have enough air to get to the Jump ." Then pushed the vacuum handle on the cockpit to Active. }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Tex chuckled as he locked his gear into place. "We don\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t even know where we\u8217\'92re headed, but this guy's sure we'll have extra. I like that." John added in "Your only saying that because you\u8217\'92re not the one watching the gauges." Tebo, already back to scanning signals, gave a brief nod. "You worry too much, John. That's why I'm here, Sit back and enjoy the ride." }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0  }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93We\u8217\'92ve reached Vacuum. We are approaching international space"Said Tau .The ship fell to the silent hum of the quantum fusion couple engine, awaiting it\u8217\'92s next vector thrust trajectories. By now they had all strapped into the holding bays in the cargo looking at one another in almost unison Tau Tex and Shai, closed their visors creating a crisp seal. Tebo, not being subject to the cold of vacuum went about his duties carefree. \u8220\'93All systems showing optimal guys, let's see if they accept our transit request\u8221\'94. }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93It\u8217\'92s too quiet\u8221\'94 said Tau, eyeing the time in her HUD. \u8220\'9310 seconds\u8221\'94, The others looked at each other in anticipation \u8220\'93Sorry just a delay in the translator\u8221\'94 chuckled Tebo. Patching through the Hail now. }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Haul carrier X15-8901\u8221\'94. There was a moment of silence. Tebo engaged the microphone, although this time his voice was not himself. It was a female operator. \u8220\'93Copy Sky Dome, I have you loud and clear Haul Carrier X15-8901\u8221\'94 over\u8221\'94 another pause between radio static over the hangar bay, \u8220\'93copy that\u8221\'94, \u8220\'93One more thing X15..your load seems off\u8221\'94.,Tebo was fast in his respones \u8220\'93Copy  control, I think it\u8217\'92s just the glare from the sun, could be throwing out your video feeds volumetric calculations, give it some time to correct itself\u8221\'94}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 In the moment the soft feminine words left tebo\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s emitter, the quantum couple of the light shield seemed to shrink inward momentarily, the light from the sun still piercing through like a blistering explosion. So much sound in the feeds of the protectants monitoring scanners didn\u8217\'92t allow precise measurements of the ship. }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The voice of the global astreroid defence systems operator was softer, kinder. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Ahh yes, we have you at the correct load estimate and ship make. Welcome to Ceres Madam.. We have your departure papers leaving Ceres station tomorrow morning at 0600\u8221\'94, \u8220\'93Copy that Sky Dome, speak again at the transit  tomorrow }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 morning, have yourself a lovely evening\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94. }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 -}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Meanwhile on the Balaenoptera.  an alarm flashed over Tors terminal froman algorithm he had implemented earlier to detect any discrepancies picked up over the chatter and volumetric scans at the planetary asteroid defence  on the sky dome Channel. }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\pard\plain \sa180\sb180\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Marcellus\u8230\'85 we have a haul carrier requesting transit through to Ceres Station. The paperwork and logistics seem fine, but there\u8217\'92s a discrepancy in the ship volumetrics upon arriving at the transit .\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93What\u8217\'92s the callsign?\u8221\'94 Said Marcellus, Tor frantically flicked the data over to the bridge monitors, displaying a hologram of the ship for Marcellus to examine.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93What are you hiding, X15-8901?\u8221\'94 Marcellus muttered, pacing across to Tor\u8217\'92s terminal and standing at his side.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93The initial volumetric scans were off, but then they corrected again,\u8221\'94 Tor explained.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93What was the light penetration from the sun? Did we get any interference?\u8221\'94 Marcellus gleaned closer in at the Hauler. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93The scan was taken at 0800 hours, right on sun set.\u8221\'94 Said Tor wiping a drip of sweat from his forehead.  \u8220\'93Hmm\u8230\'85 what percentage were the volumetrics out?\u8221\'94, \u8220\'93Two percent, sir.\u8221\'94 Tor shot back. \u8220\'93I see. That\u8217\'92s not uncommon around that time of day. And when they cleared the , did the scans correct?\u8221\'94 \u8220\'93Yes, sir.\u8221\'94 \u8220\'93Then what are you flagging it for?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Sir\u8230\'85 I deemed it necessary with the heightened security measures.\u8221\'94 Tors words trembled for a moment as they left his lips. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Hmm. I see. Fair call, Lieutenant.\u8221\'94 Tor sighed relaxing a bit more dropping his shoulders slightly. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Marcellus leaned closer to the monitor, his eyes narrowing. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Zoom in on that ship from the previous scan.\u8221\'94 Tor got back into action lifting his shoulders immediately in response to Marcellus\u8217\'92s order. his hands twisted, angling the ship\u8217\'92s hologram to a narrower viewpoint looking along the cockpit window back to the engines. Then, with a spreading gesture, he zoomed in on the model. The image, reconstructed from 32 scan viewpoints, displayed reasonable clarity. A small amount of glare could be seen on the hologram from the sensors facing the sun, scattering any distinguishable details.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Zoom in on the shaded side of the vessel,\u8221\'94 Marcellus ordered. \u8220\'93Focus on the cockpit.\u8221\'94 Tor complied, adjusting the view. \u8220\'93Sir\u8230\'85 the cockpit windows,\u8221\'94 Tor hesitated, his brow furrowing. \u8220\'93They seem to have some static in the image. I can\u8217\'92t make out the pilot.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Marcellus\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s jaw tightened as he stared at the display. \u8220\'93Something\u8217\'92s off. I want you to intercept that hauler and redirect them to the nearest inspection bay. Get a lock on them immediately as a warning if they decide to try anything funny\u8221\'94, \u8220\'93Putting it through, Commander,\u8221\'94 Tor replied, his fingers dancing across the terminal. Tor rested his hand on his Chin prying gazing deeper into the haul carriers call sign \u8220\'93X15-8901??\u8221\'94 He pondered. Then his gaze broke. A blue strobe accompanied message notification hovered across the Cockpit \u8220\'93Earth Secretary General Lady Ava Meerakavita requesting call to the bridge\u8221\'94 Marcellus queased at the notification \u8220\'93Gahh dam Technocrats, put her through Tor!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The screens hanging above the bulkheads of the bridge brought up a video feed of the Earth General Secretary for Defence, her perspective overlooking the operations table and the countless engineers and ranking officers of the bridge. They bowed their heads in respect.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Lady Ava, what graces us with your timely presence?\u8221\'94 Marcellus seemed enthusiastic initially, erring off to contempt and lethargy, like he could only afford her so much energy in the immediate urgency of the situation.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Lady Ava was enough\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 a still patience in her tone, but it was underlined with a mutual annoyance. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Would you care to update me on the most recent developments, Marcellus? Why are we firing Electron-class missiles and then target locking with warheads without my prior authorisation? I already have a political shitstorm on my hands from the previous ordnance disposed of over the lost facility.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 It\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s still unclear what exactly it is you claim you were shooting at\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 no evidence of any rogue sentient activity. Your data that was sent to my office is incomprehensible.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Marcellus sighed, \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93We felt it to be necessary considering the circumstances surrounding the last outbreak of rogue code at the facility, in order to contain any malicious codes that might otherwise infest or compromise our own system integrity. John and his team knew the details. They knew the risks associated if they meddled with old compromised systems.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93That may be so, Marcellus, but aren\u8217\'92t you curious to at least attempt to contain this so-called outbreak in a manner which values the lives of your loyal men and women that have placed their lives on the line to investigate this apparent threat?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 It seems the only threat to human life at this moment as I see it are us, in the eyes of certain parties\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8230\'85 well\u8230\'85 I can\u8217\'92t entirely agree with your methods.\u8221\'94}
\par\pard\plain \ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 -}
\par\pard\plain \sa180\sb180\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Back on the }{\f2\fs24\b0\i1 Beverly}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 , Tebo was deep into his checks, syncing the ship\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s  operations, when Kitten interrupted his focus.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Tebo, my friend,\u8221\'94 Kitten began, leaning casually against a terminal. \u8220\'93How\u8217\'92d you know the glare would buy us time?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Just enough time, my friend,\u8221\'94 Tebo replied, not even looking up. His fingers flew across the console, his focus unwavering.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 John hovered nearby, uneasy. The others had relaxed, already breaking into quiet chatter, celebrating the easy slip past the Haul inspection bay. Whatever Tebo had planned next, it seemed to them like smooth sailing\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 or at least, for now.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93What do you think it\u8217\'92s like out there?\u8221\'94 Shai asked, her voice soft as she retracted her visor back into her helmet. Her gaze shifted to Tau, curiosity in her tone. \u8220\'93I don\u8217\'92t know,\u8221\'94 Tau replied, her visor sliding back with a soft hiss. \u8220\'93Better, I hope.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 John glanced over his shoulder at them before returning his attention to the terminals. Beside him, Tebo was immersed in priming the Quantum Lock Fusion Drive for a full burn. From his forearm extended a lattice of translucent wires, intertwining seamlessly with the terminal's input ports, like the delicate roots of a tree seeking connection.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The light coursing through those threads pulsed with an almost ethereal glow, each surge alive with intent. What at first appeared rhythmic gave way to a deliberate, almost sentient pattern\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 each flicker and shift of energy a step in a complex, unseen choreography. The terminal responded in kind, its interface lighting up in a series of cascading hues, echoing Tebo\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s precision.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 It was more than input; it was symbiosis. Every motion of Tebo\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s mechanical limbs seemed less like a command and more like a conversation between the machine and its master, his movements fluid yet purposeful. The terminal's soft hum harmonised with the faint crackle of energy as if both were breathing in unison.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Something had shifted, the pattern now erratic yet purposeful, as if the Tebo itself were bracing the ship for evasive maneouvers. John\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s voice cut through the cargo hold, amplified by the PA. \u8220\'93Visors down!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The authority in his tone sent a ripple through the crew. Tau and Shai reacted instantly, their visors snapping back into place. Tex just shrugged, his still securely affixed.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Tebo smirked slightly, his hands never pausing just patiently observing unease between the others. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Buckle up, kids. Things are about to get interesting.\u8221\'94 Tex chuckled to himself. The ship had shifted. Tebo had reorented the ship facing directly for the sun, the cockpit of the Beverly exploded with hot light, as the Suns rays blinded John momentarily as his visors light sensors struggled to keep up with the sudden influx. }
\par\pard\plain \ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Shai held onto her bay cradles nervously strapping into the High G burn seat. Tex and Tau following suit. Silence broke yet again the same familiar  controller voice over the ship speakers. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Cargo Hauler X15-8901 You are to return to the inspection bay immediately, Do not alter your trajectory course. Continue onto\u8221\'94 Tebo interrupted the call over the radio \u8220\'93Copy that  Control, We appear to be experiencing control system failure, can you please send help\u8221\'94 Tebo exchanged a cheeky smile with John tilting his head in his direction. Continuing on his set trajectory \u8220\'93What the fuck are you doing Tebo.. They\u8217\'92re about to lock on us if we don\u8217\'92t turn tail and head to that bay we will be space showers for the next Hauler..\u8221\'94 John added cautiosly and more calmly after \u8220\'93We aren\u8217\'92t gunned for this fight..\u8221\'94 John\u8217\'92s voice croaked with anticipation at Tebo\u8217\'92s next move. \u8220\'93Yes the Beverly isn\u8217\'92t gunned for a full assault, but that\u8217\'92s not what we\u8217\'92re doing my friend, don\u8217\'92t worry I have a trick up my sleeve, it\u8217\'92s allll in the simulation\u8221\'94. John calmed himself Tau and Shai following his aura. \u8220\'93If you say so, Tau get me up rear defence sectors, and about face the rail cannon on our Tail so we can use the discharge force to aid our Escape, Tex I want you on rail gunner, Tau Shai Port and starboard PDC\u8217\'92s respectively, me and Tebo will handle the bowel\u8221\'94, \u8220\'93Copy that\u8221\'94 Said Tau, \u8220\'93Gahh I always take the bigseat\u8221\'94 chuckled Tex. \u8220\'93Your the only one that fits in the darn thing\u8221\'94 laughed John. The atmosphere eased for a moment now with John asserting direction. }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Johnn.. \u8221\'94 Tau seemed uneasy in her voice. \u8220\'93They have us locked, Electron Fusion Class Engine Missiles, we can\u8217\'92t outlast those kind of speeds and burn times, we will have to engage if they fire\u8221\'94 \u8220\'93Hmmm silent, and fast\u8221\'94 Tebo still seemed unphased by the apparent and imminent danger of the situation. The radio hailed once more \u8220\'93X15-8901 Change trajectory, this is you final 5 second warning, we are unable to assist at present, Kill your burn and await recovery, You have 5 seconds to comply\u8221\'94. \u8220\'93Of course Controller, I have you loud and clear, commencing burn cool down sequence\u8221\'94. John could tell the little machine man was simply trying to buy them as much time, he knew that they could not outrun missiles, He also knew they could atleast make it difficult for a rail cannon intercept  The more distance he put between them as possible. }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The cockpit of the Beverly lit up in a pulsing amber and red transition. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Incoming Missile detected\u8221\'94 pulsed in Red, \u8220\'93Missile Lock\u8221\'94, Amber. shot across the bulkhead emergency displays. The red and amber flick creating an eery anticipation in the cargo hold, yet at the front of the ship John and Tau seemed focused, determined, almost as much as Tau. \u8220\'93That cruise missile will reach us in 2 minutes if we don\u8217\'92t intercept or comply\u8221\'94. Tau was already mounting her defence setting firing vectors for the storm rail cannon mounted just behind the cockpit of the Beverly.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 She looked over to Tex \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I hope you ran your checks thoroughly " . "Smooth as a whistle. Tex replied confidently." Kitten chimed in pleasantly as always." I have created a firing sequence for you miss Vang " . Tex had just loaded and primed the storm rail"thankyon kitten" Then began climbing up into the pilot seat of the rail cannon"do you think this old girl will have enough 'charge to keep them at that range?", The Storm rail 1st guns are reliable enough. "And the new cells we updated the Bev with will go beyond parameters you humies are used to" Said Tebo}
\par\pard\plain \sa180\sb180\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 "He means to say it will work" said Tex. Pulling down the aiming visor of the cannon into his sites "how many of these fish do we have to pop" Said Tex. Tau frantically checked her HUD once again \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93One so far, we need to keep our eyes peeled. as there could be more coming. be ready" Kitten interrupted Tau "The first missile is coming into range". As soon as she spoke the Storm rail could be heard charging up. It's internal armature loading a slug into place. \u8220\'93Machine Man.. I\u8217\'92m only at 60% charge\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Kitten continued to announce."First missile intercept in 10 9, 8, 7, 6, 5, 4,.." \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Tebooo\u8221\'94 Croaked Tex his sites locked directly on the missiles nose brief silence John watched Tebo, completely unphased. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 2097 Earth Outer Orbit. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Marcellus watched on from the bridge on the Balaenoptera, the missiles data feed showing the Ice Haulers thrust plume edging closer, brighter until there was nothing but crackled static spewing colours and then the dark void of space complimented by a blinding sun. No ship debris, No camera feed connection loss, It appeared like from the camera feed as though the missile had been teleported, past the hauler. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93What in the hell happened, where are they on the Radar, No confirmed hit, but no Hauler, what the hell is going on down their Lieutenant\u8221\'94 Marcellus whipped his word around the bridge like he was herding cattle. \u8220\'93Sir, that ship it just changed shape\u8221\'94, \u8220\'93How is that even possible?\u8221\'94, \u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m not sure but I am pretty sure when we last checked we weren't hailing a science research vessel\u8221\'94 \u8220\'93What in tarnation\u8221\'94 Marcellus gleaned closer on the periscope fix of what was once Cargo Hauler X15-8901. It certainly wasn\u8217\'92t a cargo hauler anymore. \u8220\'93That ship didn\u8217\'92t change shape Tor, It\u8217\'92s dam cloaking technology, and something we\u8217\'92ve never intercepted before.. }{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "scrivcmt://CB92F2D8-5149-4489-8F16-A88517A12748"}{\fldrslt\f0\fs24\b0\i0 over half a century ago}}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Lady Ava, Do you recognize this Vessel?\u8221\'94 Marcellus zoomed in on the Beverly, a moment he allowed her to recall. \u8220\'93I Recall a certain Engineer who enticed in extraterrestrial initiatives through her work, Not approved of course by your Technocrats, off target? Wouldn\u8217\'92t I be within reasonable force to lets say decommission that project rightfully\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93And the people flying that ship Marcellus, what have they done to you\u8221\'94, \u8220\'93Insubordination of a clear directive?\u8221\'94, \u8220\'93So they should be court marshalled, not blown to oblivion?\u8221\'94 Ava rebutted, \u8220\'93Well that would be so, however do you see those PDC\u8217\'92s\u8230\'85 and the storm rail mounted on it\u8217\'92s hull. This is not a scientific vessel anymore, it\u8217\'92s a direct threat to the lives and souls on Ceres station, we have an obligation to deter and defend at all costs the lives of those on that station wouldn\u8217\'92t you agree\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93John.. What have you gotten yourself into\u8221\'94 Ava muttered under her voice with deep concern, but only so loud that Marcellus and the bridge officers could only just guess the name.  \u8220\'93And tell me Commander, when that new sleeve comes off the ice, how do you think he will feel knowing how his predecessor met his end\u8221\'94 Lady Ava recognised the name of the vessel, John\u8217\'92s horse from when he had grown up, as much as John could not remember entirely given his conditioning, Ava appreciated the deep meaning his mother had emblazoned the ship with in her discrete naming. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93What better way to set an example of what happens when you stray from a directive\u8221\'94 Marcellus smirked then carried on wi thout waiting for Ava\u8217\'92s response \u8220\'93Tor what are the lifescan readings you are picking up on that vessel. That name on the vessel\u8230\'85 I don\u8217\'92t recognise it\u8221\'94. Tor staggered immediately into action pressing keys upon his terminal to access the  scan data. \u8220\'93Loading up life-form scan data now sir\u8221\'94 The screen pulsed a loading symbol as the ships acoustic listeners also homed in on the Beverly\u8217\'92s location. \u8220\'93Sir it\u8217\'92s it\u8217\'92s showing.. 4 Human lifeforms, and one.. Well it doesn\u8217\'92t seem to show up like anything on our register, it appears, machine, like an operating system of sorts, I can\u8217\'92t tell if it is part of the ships internal control system or another individual unit, the code certainly is unlike anything I have seen before..\u8221\'94 Without hesitation Marcellus snided in his remark \u8220\'93Send everything we have, waves of 8. I want that vessel erased from the history books\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 -}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The cockpit of the Beverly lit up with the softer now yellow caution status, \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Aren\u8217\'92t we meant to be dust right now\u8221\'94 Said Shai, \u8220\'93That electron class cruise missile.. It\u8217\'92s \u8220\'93Tau gleaned closer into her Terminal\u8221\'94 It\u8217\'92s turning around.. It went straight past us? I don\u8217\'92t get it!" \u8220\'93Warning shots are always targeted at the outer burners to cripple and preserve life, instead of completely taking out the main burner and leaving potential for life support failure.. It\u8217\'92s standard operating procedure\u8221\'94 Said John. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93John\u8217\'92s correct\u8221\'94 continued Tebo \u8220\'93They hit what they thought was our port aft burner, but it was just a light illusion created by the quantum light couple cloak\u8221\'94}
\par\pard\plain \ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Tau looked up at Tebo, who was confidently perched in his cockpit chair. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93They rely heavily on image processing because of the glare zone\u8230\'85 Tebo, you\u8217\'92re a genius! They didn\u8217\'92t have the capability to focus on heat signatures because of the interference caused by the sun!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Tebo turned back and smiled. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93We\u8217\'92re not out of the clear yet. Now our cover\u8217\'92s blown, I\u8217\'92m redirect the energy from the cloaking shield to full burn on our thrusters.\u8221\'94 His connection with the terminal lit up once more, the pulses of light more erratic than before, like a storm trapped within the wires.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93What about the dummy cargo? Should we ditch that too, seeing as our cover\u8217\'92s blown?\u8221\'94 John asked, his tone cautious.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Tebo smirked. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93It may still prove useful.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I hope you\u8217\'92re right,\u8221\'94 John replied, glancing at the sensors. \u8220\'93We\u8217\'92ve got eight missiles incoming\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 warhead class 4\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 and that EMP missile? It\u8217\'92s headed straight back for us.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Tex grunted, adjusting his weapons console. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ve got the warheads in my sights. Someone do something about that EMP missile !\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Tebo\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s calm voice suddenly filled the comms. \u8220\'93Buckle in\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 we\u8217\'92re about to pull some serious G\u8217\'92s.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The plume of the Beverly didn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t erupt in flames but unfurled with precision, like the opening of a flower. The ship roared forward, its thrust perfectly controlled and deliberate.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Tex, Shai, Tau, and John groaned as their bodies strained against the intense G-forces.\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Four G\u8217\'92s and rising,\u8221\'94 John croaked, his voice tight as he struggled to breathe.\u8220\'93We\u8217\'92re about to get hit with a cocktail of adrenaline and stabilisers,\u8221\'94 Shai added, bracing herself. \u8220\'93Sit back and enjoy the ride.\u8221\'94 Said Tex like he had just opened his first beer for the night.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The ship propelled forward at a breakneck pace, closing the gap with the cruise missile that had turned back toward them. Onboard the electron class cruise missile, Tor watched on from the }{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "scrivcmt://D283AA84-BE16-4647-8599-D9EBAA563148"}{\fldrslt\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Bealenoptera}}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 , the Beverly\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s cockpit grew larger on his monitor with every passing moment, his expression frozen in disbelief at what he was watching. Ava gasped in astonishment. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0  }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93It\u8217\'92s suicide!\u8221\'94 Tau exclaimed, panic creeping into her voice. \u8220\'93We\u8217\'92ll be sitting ducks if that thing fries our engine controls!\u8221\'94, \u8220\'93Prepare to brace, comrades,\u8221\'94 Tebo said calmly. Then, without warning, he fell silent, his glowing head tilting slightly forward, as though he\u8217\'92d entered a trance.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93What the faark?\u8221\'94 Shai muttered sarcastically, her eyes darting toward Tau with concern written across her face. Tau\u8217\'92s lip curled slightly, but she said nothing. Suddenly, the burn eased, and the Beverly came to a standstill. }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The rhythmic pulses of energy that had been flowing from Tebo into the terminal had now reversed direction, coursing back into him. The lights across his visor rippled and flickered with a strange, hypnotic pattern.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Did we just cop an EMP hit?\u8221\'94 John asked, confusion colouring his tone as he scanned the terminal. \u8220\'93All systems are still operational!\u8221\'94 Tau replied, her voice matching his urgency. Her gaze shot to Tebo, who remained in his meditative state.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Slowly, he leaned forward, the glow of his head intensifying. Ripples formed across his visor, radiating outward like electrical waves. With a subtle shockwave that amplified from the nose of the Beverly, the incoming missile\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s plume flickered and died.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The missile floated lifelessly in the void, its thrust extinguished\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 a useless hunk of electronics adrift in space. Tebo re-engaged the thrusters to full blast. The missile, now just a dead cylinder, bounced harmlessly off the Beverly\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s nose like a discarded soda can.\u8220\'93Okay\u8230\'85 that\u8217\'92s a new trick,\u8221\'94 John quipped, his voice light despite the tension. Tebo turned to the left his glance fixed on John. His visor swirled with comical patterns. \u8220\'93space junk now,\u8221\'94 he shrugged seeming to grin.}
\par\pard\plain \sa180\sb180\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The missile flickered and spat about as the electron pulse plasma plume seemed to strangle what remained of it\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s banks uncontrollably. Tebo began to cite information from his play book. \u8220\'93The doctor injected a day 0 code within the manufacturing the missile systems, the code will now drain any reserve in the missile to lame it in case of recovery\u8221\'94. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Tebo's theatrics were merely compliment to the already planned dropout of the missile. "Day Zero code" Tebo said smoothly "The Dr sure has his methods\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94 Tex paused for a moment "Hmm" Sighed, and glanced at the missiles that had been tailing them getting closer and closer. The Beverlys\u8217\'92s plume burst out into a full burn thrust. The shroud of the now disposed missile slipped into the shadow of a planetary defence cannon. "Hey Cap, Do we need to be worried about those rock killers?" Tex seemed a little concerned watching it shell get tossed into the side of the cannon\u8217\'92s floating mass.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 John looked over to Tebo, Tebo seemed care free, not even concerned with the question, John shrugged looking at Tex. Kitten broke the silence like a letter opener spilling out information in what she felt would calm and focus them. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 "As far as i know planetary defence systems are not authorised for engagements where human life is at play, due to the Calibre of the rail systems engagements may also result in higher casualties due to unplanned solar fallout, at this stage a takeout of an entire ship, better more their own planetary defence cannon, this would render the loss of life unjustified\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94, Tebo chimed in, \u8220\'93What she\u8217\'92s saying amie!!,  is that as long as I close the gap, and stay relatively close and between them until I need to scoot out, they won\u8217\'92t use them\u8221\'94. Kitten concurred but continued \u8220\'93It was written into the space debris and  human intervention accord" kitten chimed confidently \u8220\'93I wouldn\u8217\'92t trust the accord if I am honest my wi Amie Kitten, we can use the turret formations as a deterrent nonetheless.\u8221\'94 \u8220\'93Isn\u8217\'92t that maximising the fallout zone for human casualties\u8221\'94 Shai interjected \u8220\'93Precisely\u8221\'94 said Tebo softly, \u8220\'93The algorithm alone wouldn\u8217\'92t allow the fallout and substantial loss of human life within certain firing trajectories. There are too many political layers to cross with that road\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Tebo seemed to smile \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I would say Kitten does raise a good point John, she also thinks with numbers and politics now, some may say she surpassed you guys in history?\u8221\'94 \u8220\'93Thank you Tebo Kitten chimed\u8221\'94 \u8220\'93I think I\u8217\'92m going to be sick\u8221\'94 said Tau, \u8220\'93Can you guys get a virtual room at a later time and just get it over with\u8221\'94 Shai joked.. }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 back on the Balaenoptera Marcellus watched on intently," gahhh!" he sighed not surprised however. "EMP directed hit, no something else perhaps?" "Correct 'Commander." Said Tor. "A direct EMP hit would have resulted in an abrupt fail-safe and subsequent explosion, it was definitely something else..", "what could it be then,?", "Day zero code is the only possibility commander electrical failure is not an element we deal with in the newer models, not with the low consumption of the quantum chips usage." "Smarter than I anticipated" Marcellus seemed almost impressed by the new development, }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 "Give me the model make of the first missile and bring up it's root code, cross check for any code implemented by Dr Wolfgang!\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94 Marcellus was powerful yet assured in his authoritative tone.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 "There!" proclaimed Marcellus. The first push of the firmware code illuminated across the bridge terminal. Dr Wolfgags initial had been assigned the the push.the code read like, }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0  \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93IF  = TRUE c SV a 1, xy2M = 100\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 "There was nothing ever mentioned in the Project of oasis commander\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94 Tor\u8217\'92s voice shattered with confusion . "So you built yourself an out it seems Wolfgang". "Interesting said Lady Ava, "How can you be so sure it was really wolfgang that wrote that code "she questioned pacing slowly over to marcellus with grace looking him dead in the eye.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Her gaze pierced his accord with inquisition. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93He was involved in the manufacturing of that release with the worker bot program! Marcellus couldn't be more certain in his tone. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 "Wasn't a rogue AI the whole reason you decommissioned the facility"." well yes." "Well if infect this Al was rogue would that not Expunge Dr wolfgang of any involvement without doubt, wouldn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t one argue that he may have been compromised " .Marcellus stood firm realining his posture after being staggered  by Lady Ava\u8217\'92s presence "while your statement is sound it doesn't override the fact that as a result of his project we now potentially stand toothless against an uncontrolled sentient Al.. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 "Well yes I suppose you have a point.. but I still believe we don't know exactly what we're dealing with here, this so called rogue Al has not attacked anyone, it looks to me like they are running in their defence at this " . Ava's statements were concise, with a touch of sincerity in her closing statement. "Yes running to this Oasis so it may seem" There was a malice in Marcellus\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s undertone, as he spoke softly but with a cutting croak. Marcellus paced the bridge.. "Tor, how long until we have and intercept on that next wave of long range pulse drives?, and tell me their date of manufacture, make sure they were after the worker-bot program. any link ups to the lost facility production lines.." The new electron class was produced 50 years after the decommission Sir. Any code affiliated with the project was completely scrapped when drives were completely wiped". Marcellus smiled. "good." Snide was ridden across his cheeks. "they won't have any system overrides planted in this wave then"}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1\cb4\highlight4 The distance between the hull of the retrofitted science cruiser beverly and the remaining 9 protectorate electron class cruise}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  missiles closed, Tebo watching on from the cockpit monitor. "No day zero easter eggs in this basket unfortunately my  heavy handed friend",Tex was still fixed his eyes locked on the formation "I got them in my sites still but I don\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t know how well a storm rail will fair against them in close range, your better off maximising PDC angles if they make it close\u8221\'94 Tex gritted his teeth focusing on the leading missile. He clenched the grip of the rail storm as he tracked the blue amberous dance of it\u8217\'92s tail, the mechanical aided mount of the Storm rail made it feel weightless upon his shoulders and hips, the cannons enclosure seemed to track his movements intuitively, he was locked in a mere thought would adjust his firing vectors. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 he focused in on the first missile ahead of the rest which formed an inverted parabolic curve approaching fast like a horseshoe of death. The outermost edges of the horseshoe were accompanied by another 3 missiles either side. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 "Their weapons firing formation has 'updated ' based on our weapons and PDC array "Said John . Tau brought up John\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s list of firing solutions taking a moment to ponder options "We'll only be able to hold of the first 6 before the outer 6 missiles will overcome our flank and take out our drive\u8221\'94. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Tex looked over to Tau with a funny look in his eyes. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Don\u8217\'92t go getting any crazy ideas big guy\u8221\'94 Said Shai. her voice with concern. "If you can get the ship wayward one side of the missiles it will tunnel our firing barrel and we might be able to focus our PDC fire from both sides of the ship into that tunnel." Said Tau smoothly with assurance "Two steps ahead of you girl, Great minds think alike" Said Tebo.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93First missile is coming into range". Without delay the rattle of PDC fire trickled through The beverly\u8217\'92s belly enticing the focus of her guardians. The sound of course just seemed like a muffled metalic clack, as sound of gas merely dissapated in the thick vacuum of space. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The missile seemed to counter Shai\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s initial PDC stream of bullets, Tex followed Shai\u8217\'92s shai\u8217\'92s fire with a Borate laced round cutting the missile off with a solid hit as a round pierced through the seemingly small payload. The missile exploded in a bright ball of light. The two missiles that had tailed behind it ran astray into the debris cloud setting off a chain reaction of bright light "3 down.. 9 to go" }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Tex seemed confident. Suddenly the ship\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s gravity shifted as the remaining missiles closed in tighter to the Beverly. }{\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cb4\highlight4 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m bringing her around.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Said Tebo. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Left side huh... closer to the earth, you trying to blindside us with the sun this time Tebo?\u8221\'94 Said John \u8220\'93We\u8217\'92re only poking behind us. We need a better angle, remember they have the sun, we have them, on our tails\u8230\'85\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Tebo seemed to smile, in the way he said it, then went quiet. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Ok I\u8217\'92ve got the remaining 9 on our starboard now,\u8221\'94 Tao seemed frustrated, \u8220\'93I can\u8217\'92t get an angle, they seem to be gaining fast.\u8221\'94 Shai let out another tail of hot lead at the grouping, clipping one of the missiles at the rear her targeting restricted by the tight angles. The missile flipped and spun out, then exploded into another light ball of oblivion fading in the distance consumed by Earth\u8217\'92s silhouette.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Preserve your rounds, we are already down to 30% on our reserve,\u8221\'94 said John \u8220\'93we need to wait for the kill tunnel.\u8221\'94\u8220\'938 to go.\u8221\'94 Shai thought to herself.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Marcellus watched on, the missiles he had sent dropping like flies, his gaze remained fixed on the terminal."How close could he get with a gunship to that damn fortified science tin can." }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Ava intervened "Even if you could get close Marcellus, you now risking protectant lives on an unknown intent."Ava was steadfast and firm in her statement. "One PDC round or even a slug through the hull at closing range, you can't guarantee that flight unscathed without collateral."}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 "Commander, we have a 90m close distance before re-fuelling with that ship's velocity, it's not like anything we've seen before," "90 meters is more than enough to shoot out their drive." said Marcellus.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Ava let out a sigh of relief twisted still sick with the feeling in her stomach like something terrible was about to unfold. Marcellus seemingly showed an initiative not to kill everyone on the ship, \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Better than his usual brute tactics\u8221\'94 she thought to herself.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 "Besides AVA, every protectant has put their acceptance on the line to uphold the federation, a re-sleave simply looks good on their service record," What remained of the relief in Ava, quickly subsided as her faint smile perished her dimples washed away in a sea of sadness. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Marcellus paused momentarily looking over at Ava's weathered skin. Then looked down at his own hands, it dawned on him for a moment, their commonality, despite their conflicting views.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 "Send in a gunship," Marcellus ordered. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 -}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93John, I\u8217\'92ve detected a gunship launch from the Balaenoptera\u8221\'94 Tebo seemed more frantic than usual, his connections to the terminals flickered in anticipation. \u8220\'93Should we be worried?\u8221\'94 John looked over to Tebo. \u8220\'93Well, I didn\u8217\'92t plan for it... it isn\u8217\'92t standard protocol\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Rogue science research vessels with PDC\u8217\'92s aren\u8217\'92t standard protocol either,\u8221\'94 John  brought up specs of the gunship launched, to his surprise the information registered against the ship was minimal, no mass speed or weapons details, completely blank, this was something entirely new. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93We\u8217\'92ll deal with the ship when it gets in range\u8221\'94 John was firm, refocusing his attention to possible solutions. \u8220\'93We still have 8 missiles coming in hot on our ass,\u8221\'94 shot Tex, his sights fixed on their plumes.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Guys, this might seem unorthodox, but it\u8217\'92s our best shot,\u8221\'94 said Tebo. \u8220\'93Get ready for an invert\u8221\'94 Despite the rapidly evolving situation  Tebo held his decorum calculated as ever. \u8220\'93Your all about to get some G\u8217\'92s\u8221\'94 without delay the Beverly pivoted as its tail began to turning about face as the rear drives hummed down, her hull nose backward, as her top now faced toward the incoming missiles.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0  The thrust gravity shoved John and his team forward then back down into his seats, the others in the rear held tight by their restraints as their bodies pushed toward the ceiling, time seemed to slow in the moment.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Tension was written all over Shai\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s face, Tex however seemed unbothered by the sudden G\u8217\'92s thinking back to his asteroid mining days. Tex refocused his sights on the missiles as they corrected their trajectory.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93They\u8217\'92re closing fast coming round now.\u8221\'94 Tex was calm, Shai watched at her sector lock, waiting for the missiles to come into sight. \u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ve got angles!\u8221\'94 She yelled. \u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ve got locks,\u8221\'94 Shai continued. \u8220\'93Same here,\u8221\'94 said Tao. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Why have they slowed?\u8221\'94 Tex observed the missiles as their plumes grew a little softer.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93They\u8217\'92ve lost tracking of our plume and the sun\u8217\'92s interference has locked up their image processors,\u8221\'94 Tebo said.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Well how convenient,\u8221\'94 said Shai, opening a short calculated burst at the group, Tao followed suit. Tex holding restraint not to join the party and preserve the ship\u8217\'92s energy reserves watching on as tracers of hot led lit up the darkness of space homing in on the plume tails of the missiles.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 One by one the plumes of the missiles vanished some simply scattering into shrapnel floating in oblivion the others going out in bright balls of light and head. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 As the incoming threats reduced to Zero across the cockpit monitors The few remaining PDC round tracers faded, the ships hold silent absorbing what little time allowed them peace to collect their thoughts in the chaos.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93We aren\u8217\'92t out of the clear yet\u8221\'94 Tebo reminded them \u8220\'93The gunship they launched\u8230\'85 it\u8217\'92s}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "scrivcmt://EB295190-2EA1-4956-962C-360B1157D7E8"}{\fldrslt\f0\fs24\b0\i0  {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cb5\highlight5 grey class.}}}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94 \u8220\'93What does that even mean,\u8221\'94 said Tex,\u8220\'93It means it isn\u8217\'92t good for us.\u8221\'94 Said John }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Brace for G\u8217\'92s\u8221\'94 Tebo announced turning the ship back around, without delay he engaged the drive. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 TTT drive engaged in attempt to misdirect then }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Tao stepped out of her PDC bay, making her way to the bridge with haste, resting her hand firmly on Tebo\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s shoulder. \u8220\'93What kind of cloaking technology does this.. Grey class have, I need to know everything.. its weaknesses, strengths, quirks.\u8221\'94 Tao seemed nervous \u8220\'93Usually we are the ones asking the questions\u8221\'94 John croaked with concern shifting his gaze to Tau \u8220\'93That\u8217\'92s not a protectant ship\u8221\'94 said John}{\f3\fs24\b1\i0  }{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93At least it is nothing like anything I have seen before\u8221\'94 John looked back to the record file, blazoned with classified clearance markers on every useful section that would otherwise inform them of what they were up against. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cb4\highlight4 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Grey class was always theoretical.\u8221\'94}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  Said Tau, pacing the cockpit. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93How come we\u8217\'92ve never heard of it,\u8221\'94 said Tex. \u8220\'93We\u8217\'92ve known for some time of a classified file base for cloaked vessels\u8221\'94 Tebo pitched in \u8220\'93Strangely enough hard evidence of the program only started popping up around the time we developed our own cloaking systems, call it a coincidence if you may, but we shouldn\u8217\'92t assume that it operates in the same way as our technology\u8221\'94 Tebo paused for a moment seeming lost, \u8220\'93Nonetheless, lets not get ahead of ourselves\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93The project was overseen by an NGO, claimed it was for far reach climate  research\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 scientific research, so we could never really get full access to it\u8217\'92s developments.\u8221\'94 \u8220\'93So secret the protectant even tried to protect themselves from internal security breaches\u8221\'94 \u8220\'93They did a darn good job of it too!\u8221\'94 Tebo concluded}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93They\u8217\'92ve never been detected in the field, the name was always urban legend, something you told the young pilots to keep them on their toes. They knew they couldn\u8217\'92t make mistakes when using something completely autonomous.\u8221\'94 Johns voice grew deeper with concern \u8220\'93Sorry to burst your bubble, but this is not helping Cap\u8221\'94 Tex groaned frustratingly, remaining vigilant he watched over the silhouette of Earth as it got smaller and smaller.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93So, you\u8217\'92re saying there is a scientific research vessel likely armed, with an AI pilot headed our way, and they\u8217\'92ve never been sighted in any mission reports.\u8221\'94\line Shai seemed composed more than anything, like she had already accepted they might not make it out of this alive.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Sounds bordering on ethical standards, Undisclosed unreleased to the public\u8221\'94 Tex grunted as he left his post, heading to the weapons rack in }{\f2\fs24\b0\i1 The Beverly\loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8217\'92s}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  cargo hold familiarising himself with the supplies and layout.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m assessing cloaking countermeasures,\u8221\'94 Tebo announced. \u8220\'93If we can throw off their magnetic cloaking fields, we may be able to detect a magnetic signature of any vessels within a certain proximity of us, if it is something man made it will resonate with our materials database identifying the compound.\u8221\'94 Tao seemed confused by Tebo\u8217\'92s approach. \u8220\'93Can\u8217\'92t we just lay low for the rest of the ride out now we\u8217\'92re clear of the missile barrage?\u8221\'94, \u8220\'93Can\u8217\'92t stalk us if they can\u8217\'92t see us,\u8221\'94 Tex agreed with Tau.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Tebo began to announce enthusiastically \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93We have one objective: get to the  undetected. A hard burn will get us there fast yet indiscreetly, a slow burn will take us almost half a day undetected, we may miss our window. The least I can do is have them tail us in the wrong direction before going dark.\u8221\'94, \u8220\'93I was wondering why you were still hot burning\u8221\'94 Said John. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Tao interrupted, \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93on a slow burn, is this girl really undetectable?\u8221\'94, \u8220\'93By protectant conventional sensor array standards I would say yes, but this new technology, I just don\u8217\'92t know.\u8221\'94, Said Tebo \u8220\'93Well at least he is honest\u8221\'94 Shai concluded calmly collecting herself while she monitored the crews vitals. There heartbeats seemed calm mostly, Except one a little bumpy. Shai watched Tex closely in his own parallel universe going over his weapon, John hadn\u8217\'92t even ordered Tex to perform weapon checks on the racked storm rails, he just trusted his judgement, even Tau caught onto this \u8220\'93John\u8230\'85\u8221\'94 Said Tau, then pausing. \u8220\'93Do you ever get the feeling that trust is almost unbreakable between you and Tex\u8221\'94, \u8220\'93He has good combat sense\u8221\'94 John concluded calmly, \u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ve seen this guy take a platoon of drones out at effective distances surpassing one thousand meters at sea depth, I wouldn\u8217\'92t doubt his targeting skills in a vacuum. \u8220\'93Tex\u8221\'94, Shai interrupted, monitoring the spike still cautiously, her eyes glistened with the prolonged gaze of concern, a second passed, which felt like a Three.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Don\u8217\'92t go getting any crazy idea\u8217\'92s now will you big guy\u8221\'94. Tex mounted the storm rail to his Mark 4 shouldering point, although this one felt different, it felt lighter \u8220\'93For precautionary measures\u8221\'94 his pupils were rigidly calm like a black still sea of glimmering lights, small specs from his helmets internal shell glimmered in the center of his eye, but all was calm, then he smiled.  On Shai\u8217\'92s HUD she could see large jawline fill the well of his helmet as he began to laugh. What\u8217\'92s so funny Tex?, \u8220\'93You wouldn\u8217\'92t believe how many times I used to love those little RC games, you know what was it called\u8230\'85 Space invaders! I spent dam hours on those things as a kid, swear it nearly sent my mother broke on her holidays\u8221\'94, Shai looked over to Tex \u8220\'93Don\u8217\'92t get me started big guy, I remember I was their, your mother did it to get you the hell away from her because you were such a pest!\u8221\'94 \u8220\'93Come on I was inquisitive\u8221\'94 Tex said in his defence..}
\par\plain {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "scrivcmt://4A92E16E-F7D8-4440-9CF0-710DD12B030C"}{\fldrslt\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Regardless, they will expose themselves the moment they open fire on our position,\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94 said Tebo confidently.\u8220\'93Precisely,\u8221\'94 Tex agreed. \u8220\'93By that point hopefully we will already be at the courier\u8230\'85\u8221\'94 Tebo concluded. \u8220\'93So, yes, don\u8217\'92t go getting any crazy ideas\u8221\'94}}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Ok, so we trick them into thinking we are headed out the back door, then hope they can\u8217\'92t trace us when we go dark, if they make themselves known we deal with it then,\u8221\'94 said John. \u8220\'93What choice do we have?\u8221\'94 said Tebo, \u8220\'93It\u8217\'92s that or we risk going up against them on our lonesome; in close proximity to the Protectant boundary, if we are caught stranded there is no telling what they\u8217\'92ll do to us.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93At least we create space between us and the blockade\u8230\'85 it\u8217\'92s our best shot.\u8221\'94 The room fell momentarily silent in hard concentration as the others contemplated the advanced humanoids logic. Tebo continued \u8220\'93One thing I know for certain, Protectant Tech can\u8217\'92t keep our pace. If we keep our hard burn we can ease off eventually and go dark, redirect our course, should put enough space between us and them, not leave use stranded, then we make a cold break tor the courier intercept\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Tau seemed still, her eyes ancious. They darted accross the ships burn parameters. She knew that their drive tech program had come to a stagnation, but that was only what she knew before being seconessoned to John\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s program. \u8220\'93I hope your right tin man\u8221\'94, she sighed. \u8220\'93Hey\u8230\'85 if we are hard burning why don\u8217\'92t we EF ping their ass at the break before we change trajectory and go cold, right as we kill the burn.\u8221\'94 John seemed puzzled by Taus logic. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 "She has a point". Tebo was delayed in his response "well I guess I hadn't really considered the value of it, call me conservation I geass. if they're going to catch us I don't see what difference knowinthere is something tailing us does, near we know they're tailing us, what information are you hoping to attain by an EM measure" }
\par\plain {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "scrivcmt://DE10F4E3-1F20-40E6-AEC1-615D09A097A3"}{\fldrslt\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Not suer I guess I just wanted to see if there was a boogey man was still hiding under my bed\u8221\'94 Said Tau. \u8220\'93If they're smart they\u8217\'92ll only perform passive tracking, image processing, light distortion, these kind of things. We won\u8217\'92t pick up anything EF related, we would need to play thier own tracking game against them\u8221\'94 Tau was quiet. She seemed perplexed, for once she didn\u8217\'92t have the answers. }}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93What kind of visual trackers do we even have on our tails? \u8221\'94 EF won\u8217\'92t work, Static Magnetic, flux field detection will likely get deflected or passed through. \u8220\'93If Something is there, magnetic will pick it up\u8221\'94. What exactly do you mean by visual trackers?\u8221\'94 Tebo chuckled for a small while, Neutrino! That will pinpoint their location if they have a nuclear drive, Can\u8217\'92t shield that.. Antimatter stands out like the hair on a cats back. \u8220\'93We have neutrino detectors?\u8221\'94 Tau scoffed. \u8220\'93Last I recall, you needed a mountain sized facility to harness anything capable of neutrino detection at feasible boundaries\u8221\'94. Tebo began to explain \u8220\'93Nuclear proliferation wasn\u8217\'92t just branding for the protectant. Their pol, even though your father made a clear objective that we be aware of nuclear matter detection, neutrino\u8217\'92s scream and scatter the moment they come into contact with nuclear material. Seems to be the only thing that\u8230\'85\u8221\'94 Tau cut the little machine man off. \u8220\'93Yes I get it, it\u8217\'92s primary school physics, but how did you get a neutrino detector to scale to fit in a ship like the Beverly?\u8221\'94 \u8220\'93Well, I didn\u8217\'92t want to tell you this, but.. Darn it, it\u8217\'92s just too dam beautiful isn\u8217\'92t it\u8230\'85\u8221\'94 Before Tebo could begin peeling back a lesson in quantum amplification drives }
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i1 (Check what would be reasonable based on science today in downscaling the size of neutrino detectors. Also supposedly this can be done from space on the surface level. Just not sub surface, hence neutrino detectors).}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  }
\par\plain {\f3\fs24\b1\i0 BEVERLY DETECTS GREY CLASS}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93One moment, I\u8217\'92m picking up an anomaly\u8221\'94. The tendrils from Tebo\u8217\'92s arm began pulsing from the cockpit terminal.  The overhead display lit up with a strange object, Tau and John squinted inquisitively, Tebo lit up the other\u8217\'92s HUD\u8217\'92s with the same view. something shrouded in bland Matt grey, like a dull half finished render flickered in electrical static over the viewports. It was completely indistinguishable from any ship or object they had previously encountered. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93What are we looking at Tebo\u8221\'94. Johns voice seethed with wary intrigue. Tebo was still pre-disposed, finalizing his assumptions, he eventually responded \u8220\'93Yes.. Grey.. grey class..96% accuracy\u8221\'94 He even seemed surprised, a the slight hesitation as he finished out his sentence, sent an uneasy silence through the Beverly. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0    }}